{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/493772-how-do-you-fit-so-many-vampires-groups-in-smaller-cities-what-ratio-do-you-follow","id":493772,"title":"How do you fit so many Vampires/groups in smaller cities, what ratio do you follow?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-27T11:48:43-07:00","id":493772,"title":"How do you fit so many Vampires/groups in smaller cities, what ratio do you follow?","content":"Hi !<br /> <br /> I'm designing my first fictional WoD city, and its neighboring towns, and the more I think about how it would work, the more I am curious as to how people usually do it.<br /> <br /> First off, the city I'm trying to develop would be located in the New England region, preferably on the very narrow seacoast along New Hampshire (since it connects to Maine and Massachusetts).<br /> <br /> My problem is that unless I pick one already existing Big city, I have a hard time respecting the 1 vampire for 100,000 people ratio that's often tossed around. I've read quite a few threads discussion the &quot;number of vampires per capita&quot; question, but unless the city is truly humongous, unless you play a lot with the ratio, it's hard to justify having so many factions, covenants and sects with so few people in each.<br /> <br /> Even New York would only have roughly 200-300 vampires at the above ratio, and Boston proper would have ~13, or up to 40 if you include the huge metropolitan area around.<br /> <br /> So how do you do it? What ratio do you use? What point is &quot;too many vampires in one area&quot; in your game? How do you manage so many covenants, sects, factions, etc. with so few vampires to play with?<br /> <br /> Also, where do you put werewolves and other supernaturals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T11:56:56-07:00","id":493817,"title":"","content":"We've had this question a lot. Like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population\">here</a>. And <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/12901-requiem-games-with-low-kindred-populations\">here</a>. And <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/370416-how-common-are-monsters\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> I don't use ratios. I put as many as their story requires, and suggest everyone else do as well. My vampire game started with 3 werewolves in the entire South Florida area, and ended with more werewolves than vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T12:06:14-07:00","id":493823,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would never respect a ratio given in any book. I pick a number that sounds comfortable for my game (I put 400 vampires and 200 Unchained in Berlin c. 1998, for instance).<br /> <br /> I understand that some people find that unsatisfying though.<br /> <br /> The best way to handle small populations is to start culling the organizations you won't be using. If you've already got a plot in mind, that makes it easy enough: just drop the Lancea et Sanctum, Ordo Dracul, or Ventrue entirely. Look to the domains in the 2E core book for examples of them playing with the Covenants and political factions in exactly that way.<br /> <br /> Next, there's not going to be much of a hierarchy. If there are only a couple of elders they'll probably dominate the power structures. There will be less political intrigue than there will be territorial disputes: coteries operate like gang cells, and are expected to get along by the leader, but obviously you need to keep up the political drama. Perhaps everybody vies for favor of the leader: if your cotery does something that's seen as weak then your neighbors will take the opportunity to try and push you out of the spotlight.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, have the city be up for grabs by two or three organizations: there's an ongoing turf-war and everybody's expected to pick a side. Neutrality means you're an acceptable target for everybody, but there could be fun had by playing the sides against each other.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T13:26:43-07:00","id":493911,"title":"","content":"I don't remember where, but where I first saw a ratio, it said that 1:50,000 is also good, if the city is of particular interest. I typically find a comfortable number somewhere between 1:50,000 and 1:100,000.<br /> <br /> 300 vampires is a ton. Remember that each vampire is probably going to end up with at least some amount of territory that is theirs. Each vampire is going to be feeding from multiple humans to sustain themselves. In that respect, I'm perfectly fine with small amounts of vampires.<br /> <br /> Really, I don't see much problem with as few as 50 vampires representing all of the factions. They're more akin to college clubs in scale than corporations, I feel. Or something like a Masonic lodge. They don't really need huge populations to function.<br /> <br /> For smaller, like Boston, there's no real reason to force every single Covenant to have representation. Maybe Boston (going with the Lovecraftian stereotype of New England) has almost entirely Ordo and maybe Circle membership. Maybe some small town of 10,000 has a single Lancea bishop as its only vampire. There's nothing wrong with that.<br /> <br /> You can certainly do the (in my opinion overplayed) advice to just &quot;do what feels right for the story,&quot; but I like the ratios mentioned because too many vampires means it's that much harder to maintain masquerade. A frugal vampire could probably survive off a single human, but when half the population is persistently anemic, the Masquerade is far too fragile. Smaller numbers help the vampires to hide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T14:13:38-07:00","id":493932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/493772-how-do-you-fit-so-many-vampires-groups-in-smaller-cities-what-ratio-do-you-follow?p=493817#post493817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've had this question a lot. Like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population\">here</a>. And <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/12901-requiem-games-with-low-kindred-populations\">here</a>. And <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/370416-how-common-are-monsters\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> I don't use ratios. I put as many as their story requires, and suggest everyone else do as well. My vampire game started with 3 werewolves in the entire South Florida area, and ended with more werewolves than vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry if that question sounded redundant. It was meant as a conjunction of two questions intersecting: given the number of potential conflictual vampire groups in existence (both PC-oriented and strictly villainous), plus the number of supernaturals both potential allies, rivals or foes, how can you fit all those divisions on so few vampires? Of course, &quot;as many as the plot requires&quot; is the default answer to it, but I would not ask the question in the first place if that was the only criteria. My world building consists of balancing the requirements of &quot;Simulationism&quot; and &quot;Narrativism&quot;, the former helping with the suspension of disbelief and the later being essential for there to be a story at all. If I put 30 vampires in a 20000 population town, it might strain disbelief a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T14:15:33-07:00","id":493934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/493772-how-do-you-fit-so-many-vampires-groups-in-smaller-cities-what-ratio-do-you-follow?p=493911#post493911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A frugal vampire could probably survive off a single human, but when half the population is persistently anemic, the Masquerade is far too fragile. Smaller numbers help the vampires to hide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since humans heal 1lethal / 2 days, and vampire needs to inflict one lethal/day to stay up he needs at least two perfectly fine humans to function. And then one day one of them get's the common cold... (this is ignoring the fact, that in most populations the vampire numbers need to be low, not in order to survive, but in order to keep hidden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T14:26:16-07:00","id":493943,"title":"","content":"Except, <i><b>Maina</b></i>, using the 1:50,000 Ration, you could feed (2 blood points per night) from the population forever, and never feed on the same person twice. Each person would be fed upon Once every 136.99 Years. Population being what it is, you would NEVER expose yourself. The Published numbers are ludicrous. Hell, even at 1:10,000 Ration, that is feeding on the same person only once every 27.4 years.<br /> <br /> I tend to design with the 1:10,000 Ratio in mind, personally. A City with 3,000,000 Residents thus contains about 300 Vampires, or so. In my current campaign setting, I have detailed about 150 of those vampires.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 04-27-2015, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T14:29:49-07:00","id":493947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/493772-how-do-you-fit-so-many-vampires-groups-in-smaller-cities-what-ratio-do-you-follow?p=493932#post493932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry if that question sounded redundant. It was meant as a conjunction of two questions intersecting: given the number of potential conflictual vampire groups in existence (both PC-oriented and strictly villainous), plus the number of supernaturals both potential allies, rivals or foes, how can you fit all those divisions on so few vampires? Of course, &quot;as many as the plot requires&quot; is the default answer to it, but I would not ask the question in the first place if that was the only criteria. My world building consists of balancing the requirements of &quot;Simulationism&quot; and &quot;Narrativism&quot;, the former helping with the suspension of disbelief and the later being essential for there to be a story at all. If I put 30 vampires in a 20000 population town, it might strain disbelief a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We've also had that conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/42052-covenant-cooperation\">Here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185242-covenants-and-your-city\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> I don't really see what's unreasonable with 30 vampires in a town of 20000. As Griautis has pointed out, vampires don't need that much blood to begin with, and for the first few decades are fine with animal blood. With the advent of subtle feeding you don't even need to tell people you're drinking from them. A vampire can hide in the attic of the Tanner family and sup quite comfortably knowing that the single men may bring home girlfriends. A gangrel can simply live near a farm and occasionally drink from cows, not requiring any humans at all. A small coterie of vampires could give a lesser bloodbond to and, with use of dominate, ensure an entire apartment building remains theirs and quiet about their presence. If just one person in that apartment building works at a slaughterhouse or hospital, they could have a whole fridge of blood restocked every week.<br /> <br /> It's not as if in a town of 300 people someone sees someone else looking more pale than usual they're going to think, 'Vampire!' and call the authorities. One of my vampires, Maw, was a patron for a small fishing community. In exchange for blood, he kept larger fishing companies out of their waters. Another just claimed the entirety of the Everglades and would, in a rather Masquerade-breaking fashion, swoop down and pick up travelers down US-1. Another vampire had a deal with werewolves, another subtly fed on monorail travelers, completely invisible. Another had her entire workplace devoted to her, another owned a strip club and partook from employees and guests. There's a lot of ways to work it so you have a balance between supply and privacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-27-2015, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T16:14:00-07:00","id":493994,"title":"","content":"From the covenant demographic ratios described for Swansea, I estimate there at least eighty vampires there. The human population is about 240,000. Chances are their Assembly is quite laissez-faire about the embrace, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T16:42:05-07:00","id":494025,"title":"","content":"First of all, so far I remember the 1:100000 ratio comes from V:tM and never worked plausible. I'm not entirely sure but I think Requiem 1.Ed. operated with a 1:20000 Ratio. But I think that is a very flexible thing. Blood may come from the population but if you have a well constructed infrastructure you may stretch that ratio. If you have a lot of tourists in a rather small town for example, or if the city is a trading place with many visitors every day, you could feed much more Vampires.<br /> The same with a Vampire Society influenced by Covenants with high abilities to either keep the masquerade or \u201cfarming\u201d humans in herds, such us Invictus or the Mivement.<br /> Last but not least, I think a higher ratio is justified if you establish a kind of medieval feudal structure. The Vampires feed in smaller towns, villages and settlements around the main City, but coming to town for business, politics and fun.<br /> <br /> And one more thing. If you take 2.Ed. Serious and gave the Ghouls more space and status you can treat them as a part of the Vampire Society (although a underprivileged one). So you could create a all night society with twice or even thrice the size with no need for more Blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T16:57:42-07:00","id":494071,"title":"","content":"For clarity's sake, from p24 in Vampire the Requiem,<br /> <br /> 'The truth is, Kindred numbers vary from city to city. In most small cities, the proportion of undead to mortals tends to be relatively low: One vampire per 100,000 or more mortals is not uncommon. In large cities, the ratio is usually nearer one vampire per 50,000 mortals. In some cities that seem to draw the Kindred for whatever reason \u2014 cities such as New York, London, New Orleans and Chicago \u2014 the ratio can be substantially higher. Most Princes don\u2019t particularly keep track. As long as the population doesn\u2019t grow so high that people take notice of the predators among them, numbers don\u2019t matter.<br /> <br /> If one were to take a worldwide average, the ratio is probably around the one-to-50,000 mark. It fluctuates so thoroughly from domain to domain that one should never assume that any given population corresponds to that figure.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T17:35:02-07:00","id":494122,"title":"","content":"You have a problem because NH has a small population. I like to start with 1:50,000 consider the metro population of a city. That number to twice that number is good for small community where everybody knows everybody else. Keep multiplying if you want less familiarity within the community. For the location you want, I would consider Boston and Portland and the area between the two cities as one big &quot;city&quot; that would have all the covenants and factions. The specific area you are focusing on might have members belonging to a covenant/faction based in one of the larger cities.<br /> <br /> Hard to say how many of the other critters without knowing if the game is Vampire with occasional outside influences or a Mixture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 04-27-2015, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T18:26:14-07:00","id":494191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/493772-how-do-you-fit-so-many-vampires-groups-in-smaller-cities-what-ratio-do-you-follow?p=493932#post493932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry if that question sounded redundant. It was meant as a conjunction of two questions intersecting: given the number of potential conflictual vampire groups in existence (both PC-oriented and strictly villainous), plus the number of supernaturals both potential allies, rivals or foes, how can you fit all those divisions on so few vampires? Of course, &quot;as many as the plot requires&quot; is the default answer to it, but I would not ask the question in the first place if that was the only criteria. My world building consists of balancing the requirements of &quot;Simulationism&quot; and &quot;Narrativism&quot;, the former helping with the suspension of disbelief and the later being essential for there to be a story at all. If I put 30 vampires in a 20000 population town, it might strain disbelief a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't sweat it it. Your not alone in your viewpoint. some of us do consider these issues. Consider that if you pull more someone stamina there are negative aspects.<br /> I did an analysis of feeding off animals and the problems with that. I think part of the ratio is as much function of the masquerade as how much blood you can pull.<br /> In other words how many people can disappear without causing a commotion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T20:50:05-07:00","id":494310,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that that even if you assume that ratio (from the very first book printed in the line, before it had had a chance to work out its own identity) as accurate, it's still practically useless for the purposes of statistical analysis. It's a simple arithmetic mean, which contrary to what most of us learned in school is not interchangeable with average. Mean is a very good indicator of average when data is normally distributed, but a terrible indicator of average when the distribution is as horribly uneven as it would be when analyzing the relationship between human populations and vampire populations. Cities with a lot of people are going to have a lot more vampires than 1:100,000 and rural areas with a lot of space and not a lot of people are going to have a lot fewer vampires. What you really want to look at is population density. The more people you've got per square foot, the more vampires you'll have per person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T23:59:10-07:00","id":494452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From the covenant demographic ratios described for Swansea, I estimate there at least eighty vampires there. The human population is about 240,000. Chances are their Assembly is quite laissez-faire about the embrace, but still. </div> </div> </div>The other point of comparison is Tokyo which has a population of about 13 million and about 300 vampires if I remember right, and is called out as one of the largest vampire populations.<br /> <br /> I don't think human population has all that much relation to the kindred population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T02:56:30-07:00","id":494559,"title":"","content":"well I think it's unreasonably unfair to calculate the base usage of vampire vitae as 1/night. After all, any wound requires vitae, a lot of disciplines require blood too. And also, someone in these forums have said this, and I've kinda stolen it to use in my game, but it's really a great point on this topic. It basically comes down to this: with the vampire longevity, most of them see a war, or two. Or famine, or disease or something equally widespread. That's when the vampire population must be able to survive without breaching masquerade. Thinking that such a time won't come is naive at best (history tells us that almost all centuries had a war... and elders know this. That's why they don't want overpopulation, because they know that once catastrophes roll around back into town, they'll need to survive in those harder conditions and preserve the masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T05:07:52-07:00","id":494613,"title":"","content":"I use the 1:50k as a benchmark. A very rough benchmark. As others have said, population density is more important than the raw numbers, and be sure to keep in mind transient population. A college town with 60k permanent residents can actually support quite a few more vampires comfortably when the three universities in town are cracking along.<br /> <br /> As an example, the Chicago metropolitan area is about 10 million people, giving you a rough vampire population of 200. In my Chicago game I have around 80 vampires in some level of solid existence. That accounts for characters who are only very rough sketches of a one or two sentence blurb and a name, to staple NPCs the players interact with regularly. That gives me a ton of wiggle room to introduce new characters, seed stories, and have faces in crowds for a dramatic Elysium, all while remaining within the bounds of suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> Yeah, dropping 5 vampires into a rural town of 15,000 is not going to work in most circumstances. You can still have those kinds of situations, you just need to take a few minutes to think about, &quot;Okay, how do these yahoos feed themselves without blowing their cover?&quot;<br /> <br /> I like Griautis' point above, as well. Bear in mind that while everything is plugging along with no problems you can get away with packing more vampires into a given population. When something happens like a war, natural disaster, whatever, you're going to have a huge problem on your hands. That would be an interesting situation to run through. It's like avoiding making a budget because you have plenty of money, and no problems paying off whatever you need. One breakdown where your car needs major work and you may be screwed. See kids? Always make a blood budget!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T05:28:14-07:00","id":494642,"title":"","content":"Using Boston as an example New England city, you've only got about 650k population in Boston itself to work with, but when you take the surrounding area of suburbs into account that number jumps to 7.6 million. That's a very workable number. Remember that you can have vampires living in relatively close proximity as long as feeding is more regulated or at least careful. Maybe in your city feeding grounds are ruthlessly patrolled, and Kindred citizens of the domain are only cleared to feed in certain areas, ensuring that the drain on the blood supply is sufficiently spread out. <br /> <br /> Herd poaching, vessel smuggling, feeding ground claim-jumpers, Prince-edict smackdowns on the folks who do those things, these are things that make vampire go 'round. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for other supernaturals, I honestly don't worry about the strict population numbers so much when I'm running a vampire game. I keep it vague as far as the players are concerned, and I only bother with a very rough sketch of what is where for myself. If you really need hard numbers to keep things tidy, I don't think there's too much overlap in supernatural population as far as any kind of supers-to-mortal ratio. None of the other supers are competing with the vampires for blood (territory and such is another concern, but lets stick with the main issue of feeding without shredding the Masquerade) so the ratio isn't impacted by mages, or changelings. <br /> <br /> That said, I love having other supernaturals present in my games, no matter the game I'm running. The focus stays on whatever that game is, of course, but I love the cosmopolitan nature of the shadows in the WoD, and I think it's important that the characters realize on occasion that they're fish in a very big, very dark pond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:37:57-07:00","id":501950,"title":"","content":"It depends if you want your players to feel like a conspiracy of supernatural folk or like isolated monsters. Dwindling the vampire population lets you focus on the more monstrous aspects of your player's characters, whereas a larger vampire population makes the story more political / conspiring.<br /> <br /> That's what I find, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T14:01:19-07:00","id":510168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/493772-how-do-you-fit-so-many-vampires-groups-in-smaller-cities-what-ratio-do-you-follow?p=493817#post493817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've had this question a lot. Like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population\">here</a>. And <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/12901-requiem-games-with-low-kindred-populations\">here</a>. And <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/370416-how-common-are-monsters\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> I don't use ratios. I put as many as their story requires, and suggest everyone else do as well. My vampire game started with 3 werewolves in the entire South Florida area, and ended with more werewolves than vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I'm hosting a Victorian era game set in Newfoundland. There's between 20-30 vampires, and how many people? Beats me. Feeding scarcity and Kindred-overpopulation are themes of the campaign so all players know that the Kindred-Kine ratio is messed up in this place, but the exact ratio has never mattered for gameplay purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T02:01:39-07:00","id":516881,"title":"","content":"I've thought about it some and as soon as there are enough people that blood supply is plentiful, I think you can easily go up to 0.5% of the population. I grew up in a small geographic area with a population density around 55/sq mi and I never met anyone of a race in the 0.31-0.66% range. I didn't go looking, but I doubt they were hiding either. I think there could be over 1000 hidden away in New Hampshire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T03:36:20-07:00","id":516916,"title":"","content":"I use the 1:10000 ratio to ballpark about 800 vampires in London, although in actual play I use 600 as the number so the PCs have easier access to during privalleges. But I also have vampire populations as being less static than normal, it's not unheard of for the prince to send a representative to another city because it's normally less than a night's drive away.<br /> <br /> PCs can expect to meaningly interact with less than a tenth of the full 600, because there's only so much that I can prepare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T04:01:20-07:00","id":516923,"title":"","content":"I'd it were me (which for my cities (Oklahoma City, and Tulsa), it is) is work out the vampires per state (or equiv. in that country) and then distribute them almost entirely to the large cities \u00b110%. <br /> <br /> Then when that number is 'low' realise that the VtR book says there should be no nameless vampires (or so previous VtR ST told me) and be thankful you're only stating 80.<br /> <br /> Put a prince in each city, and have the other covenants be side players. So I'm having Invictus vs Carthians with a powerful Ordo Dracul elder plotting, a LS minor, slightly defunct group, and the Circle acting from the shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T09:53:15-07:00","id":524553,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Vampire populations being small. It really gets across the point of claustrophobia (think Sartre's &quot;No Exit&quot;, hell is a dozen other Kindred for eternity), the desire to create more vampires for companionship (because all the other suckers suck), and the problem of having made enemies with one of the 5 elders in the City. It's like working at a really small company, with a boss that hates you, and co-workers who want to see you fail. You want to quit, but being unemployed won't work for you, you have a serious health condition (needing to drink blood) and you can barely afford it even with the 'health insurance' it provides.<br /> <br /> Add to this the fact that Vampires in a small City/less densely populated region are essentially boxed into their domains makes things even worse. Over the centuries you come to know every street corner and alley. You know all the best hunting spots..... and that's it. That's your world from now until you meet your demise sometime between tonight and eternity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5106-umoja","name":"Umoja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T12:43:07-07:00","id":526943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Umoja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/493772-how-do-you-fit-so-many-vampires-groups-in-smaller-cities-what-ratio-do-you-follow?p=524553#post524553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the desire to create more vampires for companionship (because all the other suckers suck), and the problem of having made enemies with one of the 5 elders in the City. It's like working at a really small company, with a boss that hates you, and co-workers who want to see you fail. You want to quit, but being unemployed won't work for you, you have a serious health condition (needing to drink blood) and you can barely afford it even with the 'health insurance' it provides.</div> </div> </div> </div>The corporation model was used at some point to explain why vampires are all so shitty to each other. The CEO is immortal, the board is immortal, your boss(es) are immortal, your subordinates are immortal, and the company <i>keeps hiring</i>. There's no room for growth unless someone is killed, and everybody higher up the hierarchy is older and smarter and more powerful than you, and the employees below <i>you </i>feel <i>just the same</i>.<br /> <br /> Even on your own tier, take the occasional office romance gone awry, the odd rivalry, any misunderstandings, accidents, or conflicts of personality, and let them marinate for decade after decade... your options are deal, spend all your time hiding in the toilet, or making a dangerous trip through unknown streets to another company where everything is exactly the same <i>but you've lost all seniority</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T12:23:15-07:00","id":527978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Umoja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/493772-how-do-you-fit-so-many-vampires-groups-in-smaller-cities-what-ratio-do-you-follow?p=524553#post524553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Vampire populations being small. It really gets across the point of claustrophobia (think Sartre's &quot;No Exit&quot;, hell is a dozen other Kindred for eternity), the desire to create more vampires for companionship (because all the other suckers suck), and the problem of having made enemies with one of the 5 elders in the City. It's like working at a really small company, with a boss that hates you, and co-workers who want to see you fail. You want to quit, but being unemployed won't work for you, you have a serious health condition (needing to drink blood) and you can barely afford it even with the 'health insurance' it provides.<br /> <br /> Add to this the fact that Vampires in a small City/less densely populated region are essentially boxed into their domains makes things even worse. Over the centuries you come to know every street corner and alley. You know all the best hunting spots..... and that's it. That's your world from now until you meet your demise sometime between tonight and eternity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget only the first person to a specific shop can be certain of getting enough food for the night without causing the shop to close, and you likely have to use a new shop tomorrow night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/493772-how-do-you-fit-so-many-vampires-groups-in-smaller-cities-what-ratio-do-you-follow?p=526943#post526943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The corporation model was used at some point to explain why vampires are all so shitty to each other. The CEO is immortal, the board is immortal, your boss(es) are immortal, your subordinates are immortal, and the company <i>keeps hiring</i>. There's no room for growth unless someone is killed, and everybody higher up the hierarchy is older and smarter and more powerful than you, and the employees below <i>you </i>feel <i>just the same</i>.<br /> <br /> Even on your own tier, take the occasional office romance gone awry, the odd rivalry, any misunderstandings, accidents, or conflicts of personality, and let them marinate for decade after decade... your options are deal, spend all your time hiding in the toilet, or making a dangerous trip through unknown streets to another company where everything is exactly the same <i>but you've lost all seniority</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The company doesn't even pay for your training.<br /> <br /> Don't forget, you can join the corporation that claims to be getting rid of the CEOs but is actually sticking it's own in charge, decide to become a freelancer that nobody likes, or join the group that'll let you pick your own work, as long as you don't care if it's moral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 05-25-2015, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T14:22:56-07:00","id":528092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/493772-how-do-you-fit-so-many-vampires-groups-in-smaller-cities-what-ratio-do-you-follow?p=527978#post527978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The company doesn't even pay for your training.<br /> <br /> Don't forget, you can join the corporation that claims to be getting rid of the CEOs but is actually sticking it's own in charge, decide to become a freelancer that nobody likes, or join the group that'll let you pick your own work, as long as you don't care if it's moral.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how his comparison works. The company is the All Night Society. yeah, you can move between different departments (Covenants) and you can either be a mail boy running around the place with no real place (Unaligned), but the only way to switch the company, is to skip towns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T22:48:05-07:00","id":528555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/493772-how-do-you-fit-so-many-vampires-groups-in-smaller-cities-what-ratio-do-you-follow?p=494452#post494452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The other point of comparison is Tokyo which has a population of about 13 million and about 300 vampires if I remember right, and is called out as one of the largest vampire populations.<br /> <br /> I don't think human population has all that much relation to the kindred population.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is such a silly, minor point. But I figure I should bring it up: <br /> <br /> When I was first writing Tokyo, I wrote it as 1,000. But, in my actual draft, I reduced it because that sounded really high. <br /> <br /> In retrospect, I wish I would have gone with 1,000. It's how I run it now. In fact, I specifically have some of the locals refer to &quot;the thousand&quot; instead of &quot;Kindred&quot;, and the local myth is that it's exactly 1,000, and has been exactly 1,000 since the end of the Edo Jidai.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T22:54:16-07:00","id":528561,"title":"","content":"Duly noted for the next time I try for Tokyo.<br /> <br /> (THe previous time flopped)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T03:14:15-07:00","id":528676,"title":"","content":"That makes a lot of sense. I did think it was a bit odd when I read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}